  "id": "chunk_33",
  "chunk": "although the established performance suggests little to no contamination. Our\nqualitative analysis draws on illustrative examples rather than systematic analy-\nsis across all conversation logs, and we did not systematically explore alternative\nprompt formulations that might improve performance. These limitations sug-\ngest our findings should be viewed as raising questions about LLM reasoning\ncapabilities exemplified through the gameZorkrather than providing definitive\nanswers. We present this work to spark discussion and encourage follow-up\nstudies\n7 Conclusions and Future Research\nThis study evaluated whether state-of-the-art Large Language Models (LLMs)\ndemonstrate genuine problem-solving capabilities through their performance on\nZork, a text-based adventure game that requires spatial reasoning, planning, and\nadaptive learning. Our findings reveal substantial limitations in current LLMs’\nreasoning abilities that raise fundamental questions about their path toward",
